IaaS, PaaS & SaaS
Cloud Deployment Models
1. Cloud Service Models

Cloud services are generally divided into three major models:

IaaS — Infrastructure as a Service

Provides infrastructure as a service.

You get resources such as:

Virtual Machines
Storage
Networking
CPU & Memory

Example: Amazon EC2

Hardware → Managed by Cloud Provider
OS       → Managed by User
Apps     → Managed by User

PaaS — Platform as a Service

Provides a ready-to-use platform for developing and deploying applications.

The provider manages the infrastructure and operating system, while the developer focuses mainly on the application.

Example: AWS Elastic Beanstalk

SaaS — Software as a Service

Provides complete software through the internet.

The provider manages almost everything, while the user simply uses the application.

Examples:

Gmail
Google Docs
Microsoft 365.md
